# Blubber-OS cloud config (Academy waitlist + entitlements)
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are safe to expose
# client-side — that is what the anon key is for. Row Level Security on the
# `waitlist` table only allows anon INSERT (no read/update/delete), and the
# `entitlements` / `otp_codes` tables allow the anon role NO access at all —
# see supabase/migrations/20260721124242_create_waitlist_entitlements_otp.sql.
#
# STATUS (2026-07-21): the `blubber-os` Supabase project has NOT been created
# yet — org's free-tier plan already has 2 active projects (nitez-dev, quari),
# which is the max for a Free-plan org. Creating a 3rd active project needs
# ONE of these from Dame first, both dashboard-only (no CLI command exists):
#   1. Pause an existing active project: open its Settings > General page in
#      the Supabase dashboard and click "Pause project" (reversible, ~30s).
#      https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/shdarhljvdtwciiihawi/settings/general (nitez-dev)
#      https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/skmtwlspzlbbayctptpp/settings/general (quari)
#   2. Upgrade the org to a paid plan (needs a payment method on file):
#      https://supabase.com/dashboard/org/xfqfzwgeipvzudzruonw/billing
# Once either is done, the rest of the deploy is scripted and ready to run:
#   1. supabase projects create blubber-os --org-id xfqfzwgeipvzudzruonw \
#        --region us-east-1 --db-password <generate one>
#   2. supabase link --project-ref <new-ref>
#   3. supabase db push                      (applies supabase/migrations/*.sql)
#   4. supabase functions deploy waitlist-signup
#      supabase functions deploy request-otp
#      supabase functions deploy verify-otp
#      supabase functions deploy shopify-webhook
#   5. supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=... --project-ref <new-ref>
#      (Shopify secrets go in once Dame sets up that webhook — see the
#      comment block at the top of supabase/functions/shopify-webhook/index.ts)
# Then replace the two placeholders below with the real values from the new
# project's Settings > API page, and mirror them into a local .env.local
# (gitignored, never commit it).

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
